WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.800
NOW, MOVIES BEGIN WITH A
SCREENPLAY, EITHER AN ORIGINAL

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.390
STORY OR ONE ADAPTED FROM
PREVIOUS WORK.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:11.080
AND AFTER SO MUCH ISOLATION, WE
WANTED TO GET TO KNOW OUR NOMINEES

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.160
SO, HERE ARE A FEW THINGS
WE LEARNED.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.140
THE WRITER/DIRECTOR OF
"JUDAS AND THE BLACK MESSIAH,"

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.890
SHAKA KING -- THAT'S MY COUSIN.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.679
IT'S NOT, BUT IN 
MY HEAD, HE IS.

00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:29.779
HIS FIRST MOVIE JOB WAS
AN EXTRA ON A FILM CALLED

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:32.870
"30 DAYS," DIRECTED BY
JAMAL JOSEPH,

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.219
A FORMER BLACK PANTHER.

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:37.570
AND FOR CO-WRITER
WILL BERSON,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.150
BEING THE OFFICE MANAGER
FOR JOHN LEGUIZAMO'S

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:45.199
LOWER EAST SIDE FILMS STOKED THE
FIRE IN HIM TO TELL HIS STORIES.

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:48.740
AND FOR CO-WRITER KENNY LUCAS,
WATCHING "CITY OF GOD" IN

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.679
COLLEGE INSPIRED HIM TO BE A
FILMMAKER INSTEAD OF GETTING A

00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:54.809
PHD IN PHILOSOPHY.

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:56.780
AND HIS
BROTHER KEITH LUCAS WAS

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:00.899
IN LAW SCHOOL WHEN HE
REALIZED HIS LOVE OF FILM.

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:04.680
LEE ISAAC CHUNG,
WRITER OF "MINARI"

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.590
WHOSE FIRST FILM JOB WAS
PRODUCING EDUCATIONAL FILMS

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:10.270
IN NEW YORK,
REMEMBERS SEEING "E.T."

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.420
FOR THE FIRST TIME AS A CHILD.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.960
STANDING UP WIDE-EYED IN THE
MOVIE THEATER THE ENTIRE TIME.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.240
THAT IS SO ADORABLE.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.710
OH.
AND EMERALD FENNELL, GIRL.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:27.750
YOU TOOK TIME OFF FROM PLAYING
CAMILLA BOWLES IN "THE CROWN" TO

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.380
WRITE, PRODUCE, AND DIRECT
"PROMISING YOUNG WOMAN”

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:37.490
WHILE YOU WERE SEVEN MONTHS
PREGNANT DURING A 23-DAY FILM SHOOT.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:44.450
GIRL, YOU EARNED THE
TITLE OF THAT FILM.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:48.400
DARIUS MARDER SUPPORTED
HIS TEN-YEAR JOURNEY TO MAKING

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.430
"SOUND OF METAL" WITH A
SUSHI CATERING BUSINESS IN VERMONT.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:55.789
HIS CO-WRITER BROTHER,
ABRAHAM MARDER

00:01:55.789 --> 00:01:58.830
WAS A MUSICIAN AND COMPOSER.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:03.469
AND CO-WRITER DEREK CIANFRANCE'S
FIRST JOB WAS A FRIEND'S GET

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:08.259
RICH QUICK SCHEME FILMING DOGS'
FACES TO PUT ON COFFEE CUPS

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:10.009
CALLED PUPPY MUGS.

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:14.209
DEREK, LET ME GET ONE OF THOSE MUGS.

00:02:14.209 --> 00:02:15.209
YES.

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:20.220
AND AARON SORKIN, WRITER/DIRECTOR
OF "THE TRIAL OF THE CHICAGO 7"

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:26.930
HE STARTED HIS CAREER IN MOVIES
BY RIPPING TICKETS

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.459
AND MAKING THE POPCORN
IN HIS NEIGHBORHOOD THEATER.

00:02:30.459 --> 00:02:34.200
SEE, YOU NEVER KNOW, THE GUY
SERVING THE POPCORN COULD BE

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.959
THE NEXT AARON SORKIN.

00:02:37.959 --> 00:02:42.300
AND THE OSCAR GOES TO --

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.300
EMERALD FENNELL,
"PROMISING YOUNG WOMAN”

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.744
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:03:03.607 --> 00:03:05.311
OH, MY GOSH.

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:07.669
OH, THEY SAID WRITE A SPEECH.

00:03:07.669 --> 00:03:08.902
AND I DIDN'T, BECAUSE I JUST

00:03:08.902 --> 00:03:10.802
DIDN'T THINK THIS WOULD EVER
HAPPEN, AND I'M GOING TO BE

00:03:10.802 --> 00:03:12.159
IN TROUBLE WITH
STEVEN SODERBERGH.

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:13.159
I'M SO SORRY.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:16.100
I DON'T WANT HIM TO
BE CROSS WITH ME.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:23.526
OH, MY GOD, HE'S SO HEAVY
AND HE'S SO COLD.

00:03:23.526 --> 00:03:27.420
SO THE ONLY SPEECH I EVER
WROTE WAS WHEN I WAS 10.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:31.450
I HAD A LOOK TO SEE IF THERE
WOULD BE ANYTHING USEFUL FROM IT

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.720
BUT UNFORTUNATELY, I MOSTLY
THANKED ZACK MORRIS

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:37.840
FROM "SAVED BY THE BELL," WHO WAS
MY VERY SUPPORTIVE HUSBAND.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.599
UNFORTUNATELY, HE HASN'T BEEN AS
MUCH A PART OF MY LIFE AS I'D HOPED.

00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:46.019
AND SO THAT SPEECH
IS NOT THAT USEFUL

00:03:46.019 --> 00:03:50.900
BUT ALL I CAN SAY IS, TRYING
VERY HARD NOT TO CRY,

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.750
WHICH IS VERY DIFFICULT
AS AN ENGLISH PERSON

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:56.269
BECAUSE YOU DON'T CRY EVER.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:59.530
THIS FILM WAS MADE BY THE MOST
INCREDIBLE PEOPLE IN THE WORLD,

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:03.280
WHO MADE IT IN 23 DAYS

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:07.680
AND BROUGHT THEIR COMPLETE
GENIUS AND LOVE AND HUMOR TO IT.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.770
AND I HAVE SO MANY
PEOPLE TO THANK.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.549
I FEEL MORTIFIED THAT
I'M HERE BY MYSELF

00:04:11.549 --> 00:04:14.910
WHEN IT'S NOT JUST MY
JOB AT ALL.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.480
I WANT TO THANK CAREY MULLIGAN,
FOR BEING NOT ONLY THE MOST

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:22.000
TALENTED PERSON IN THE WORLD,
BUT THE KINDEST AND FUNNIEST.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.480
I WANT TO THANK THE PRODUCERS
FOR STANDING BEHIND THIS FILM ALWAYS

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.660
AND YOU KNOW NEVER GIVING UP.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.928
AND LUCKY CHAP, FOCUS,
FILM NATION,

00:04:33.928 --> 00:04:37.220
THE CAST AND THE CREW, THE
GREATEST IN THE WORLD,

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.800
THE KINDEST IN THE WORLD.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.260
THEY JUST MADE ME LOOK GOOD.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.295
AND AGAIN, I'M JUST SO GRATEFUL.

00:04:42.295 --> 00:04:44.064
FINALLY, MY FAMILY.

00:04:44.064 --> 00:04:46.000
MOM, DAD, COCO.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.000
OH.

00:04:47.465 --> 00:04:49.426
MY HUSBAND, CHRIS.

00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:52.940
COME ON, COME ON.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:56.550
OUR SON, WHO DID NOT ARRIVE
UNTIL A COUPLE OF WEEKS AFTER

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.180
SHOOTING, THANK GOD, BECAUSE I
WAS CROSSING MY LEGS

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.310
THE WHOLE WAY THROUGH.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:02.480
SO, THANK YOU ALL SO MUCH.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.490
STEVEN, I HOPE THAT
WAS ALRIGHT!

